    whatToExpect: [
      'Liquid damage is the one fault where what you do in the first half hour matters more than anything we do afterwards. Shut the machine down properly if you can, or hold the power button until it goes off if you cannot. Unplug the charger. Do not press the power button again to see whether it still works — that is the single most common way a repairable spill becomes a dead logic board, because powering a wet board is what shorts it. Leave it closed and tented upside down so liquid drains away from the board rather than into it, and call us.',
      'Ignore the rice. It does nothing useful, it puts starch and dust into the ports, and the days spent waiting for it to "dry out" are days corrosion is spreading across the board. Liquid damage is not really a drying problem — it is a corrosion problem. Water carries salts and sugars that keep eating into the board long after the surface feels dry, which is why a laptop that worked fine for two days after a spill can die on the third.',
      'Because the clock matters, we treat spills as emergencies and will always try to see you the same day anywhere in Greater London. Proper liquid work means the board comes out, gets inspected under a microscope, and is cleaned in an ultrasonic bath rather than wiped — corrosion sits in places you cannot reach with a cloth. That needs our workshop, so this is one repair we will normally take away, and we tell you that upfront rather than after we arrive.',
      'We will always be honest with you about the odds, because they vary enormously. A splash of water caught in the first hour is very often a full recovery. A sugary drink or alcohol left for a week is a different conversation, and sometimes the right answer is to stop paying for the repair and recover your data instead. The diagnosis is free, we quote before any work, and if we cannot fix it you pay nothing.',
    ],
    faqs: [
      { q: 'I just spilled water on my laptop — what should I do first?', a: 'Shut it down immediately, or hold the power button until it switches off. Unplug the charger. Do not press the power button again to check whether it works. Leave it closed and standing tented upside down so liquid runs away from the board. Then call us on 07378 349222 the same day — the first thirty minutes genuinely decide the outcome.' },
      { q: 'Does the rice trick work?', a: 'No. Rice does not pull liquid out of a sealed laptop chassis, and it adds starch and dust to the ports while you wait. Worse, the delay is the real damage: liquid damage is corrosion rather than dampness, and corrosion keeps spreading every day the board goes uncleaned. Getting the board cleaned properly is the only thing that stops it.' },
      { q: 'My laptop still works after the spill — do I need anything done?', a: 'Yes, and this is the case people most often regret leaving. A machine that survives the first few days is not in the clear; the salts and sugars in the liquid are still corroding the board, and failures weeks later are common. Getting it opened and cleaned while it is still working is far cheaper than a board repair afterwards.' },
      { q: 'Can you repair liquid damage at my home?', a: 'Not properly, and we would rather say so. Real liquid work means removing the board and cleaning it ultrasonically under a microscope, because corrosion gets into places you cannot wipe. That needs our workshop equipment, so we collect the machine, keep you updated, and return it fully tested. Everything else about the service is the same — free diagnosis, quote first, no callout charge.' },
      { q: 'Will I get my data back if the laptop cannot be saved?', a: 'Usually, yes, and they are two separate questions. In many spills the storage is completely unharmed even when the machine will not power on, because the damage is elsewhere on the board. If the repair is not viable we will tell you and go through data recovery instead, so you at least get your files back.' },
      { q: 'What does liquid damage repair cost?', a: 'It depends on what the liquid reached, so the diagnosis is free and the quote comes before any work — our £120 per hour labour plus any parts the board needs. Sugary drinks and alcohol are more aggressive than water and often mean more work. If we cannot recover the machine, there is nothing to pay.' },
    ],
